  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.3",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $G=A_n$ or $S_n$ and let $H,K$ be soluble subgroups of $G$. For all sufficiently large $n$, can we always find an element $x\\in G$ such that $H\\cap K^x=1$? Does this hold for all $n\\geqslant 21$?",
